record(s,t,r,d,inv,"This leaf continues scan 141's compactness paragraph, cancels an attempted converse, and treats (iii)⇒(iv) through characters and Galois actions. The field lattice and character-lattice diagram are retained with their written inclusion signs. The text defines G using Gal(Ktilde/K), while its margin labels G on the Ktilde/Q connection; both labels remain. It also writes H in the final trivial-action sentence, after P in the preceding one. Check 143.N1: for the finite set I_K, the map from the free abelian group on P-orbits to Z[I_K], sending an orbit basis element to the sum of its members, identifies Z[P\\I_K] with Z[I_K]^P: invariant coefficients are constant on each orbit and the orbit supports are disjoint. This checks the displayed invariant-module identity only; it supplies no proof of the full compact-torus argument. The new diagonal inclusion in the diagram follows its curved ink, not an inferred arrow. Archive number 142.",doubts=doubts,notation=[['Finite permutation lattice','Z[I_K]; lower diagram Z(I_L)','143','Square and round delimiters vary in the ink and are retained.'],['P, Q, H','G/P; G/Q; H on K/L edge','143','The repeated P bowl and Q tail distinguish these glyphs.']],hand=['A rotated subset sign can appear as a single curved stroke between two diagram rows. Both witnesses omit the diagonal relation below N.','Separate live lines run between long cancellations; H’s broad struck wrapper suppresses the centrality and quotient insertions.','The Q tail survives even under the lower-margin hatching.'],abbreviations=[['ss-gpe','sous-groupe (reading uncertain)'],['car.','caractères'],['coeff','coefficients'],['ext.','extension'],['grpe','groupe'],['gde','grande'],['ss-ext.','sous-extension'],['trivialmt','trivialement'],['hom','homomorphismes']],events=[['143.N1','targeted proof check','Orbit-sum map e_O ↦ sum over i in O of e_i is an isomorphism onto the P-invariants; coefficients are constant on the orbits.']])
